{"tool_name":"rabbittclust","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"rabbittclust","home":"https://github.com/RabbitBio/RabbitTClust","license":"BSD-3-Clause","summary":"Enabling fast clustering analysis of millions of bacteria genomes with MinHash sketches.","addition_date":"2024-01-10T10:54:30.645236Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:22:35.446679Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:rabbittclust","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"weiguo.liu@sdu.edu.cn","name":"Weiguo Liu","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"zekun.yin@sdu.edu.cn","name":"Zekun Yin","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3432"},{"term":"Dimensionality reduction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3935"},{"term":"Genome assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0525"},{"term":"Genome indexing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3211"}]}],"name":"RabbitTClust","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-023-02961-6","metadata":{"abstract":"We present RabbitTClust, a fast and memory-efficient genome clustering tool based on sketch-based distance estimation. Our approach enables efficient processing of large-scale datasets by combining dimensionality reduction techniques with streaming and parallelization on modern multi-core platforms. 113,674 complete bacterial genome sequences from RefSeq, 455 GB in FASTA format, can be clustered within less than 6 min and 1,009,738 GenBank assembled bacterial genomes, 4.0 TB in FASTA format, within only 34 min on a 128-core workstation. Our results further identify 1269 redundant genomes, with identical nucleotide content, in the RefSeq bacterial genomes database.","authors":[{"name":"Liu W."},{"name":"Niu B."},{"name":"Schmidt B."},{"name":"Wei Y."},{"name":"Xu B."},{"name":"Xu X."},{"name":"Yan L."},{"name":"Yin Z."},{"